c/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133756453,imgsize-1284051.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US House passes bill to stop federal funding of universities boycotting Israel]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133756505.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The US House has approved a bill aimed at halting federal support for universities that boycott Israel, marking a significant political shift that now awaits Senate approval. The vote reflected a mostly partisan divide, with some Democrats voicing concerns about free speech implications. Amid escalating protests against Israel's actions in Gaza, supporters assert that the legislation addresses antisemitism, a claim contested by demonstrators who disagree with its intent.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-house-passes-bill-to-stop-federal-funding-of-universities-boycotting-israel/articleshow/133756505.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-house-passes-bill-to-stop-federal-funding-of-universities-boycotting-israel/articleshow/133756505.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T13:39:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133756611,imgsize-124928.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 2023, Princeton researchers tested radiative cooling, keeping a building 3.9°C cooler]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133754059.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers tested a building's ability to stay cooler than outside air naturally.  A special roof released heat towards the sky, while airflow moved air through openings.  This passive system kept the test box significantly cooler than the prevailing outdoor temperature.  The experiment demonstrated radiative cooling working with thermal mass and temperature-driven ventilation.  This approach offers a way to cool buildings without mechanical systems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2023-princeton-researchers-tested-radiative-cooling-with-natural-ventilation-and-thermal-mass-keeping-a-building-3-9c-below-outdoor-air/articleshow/133754059.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2023-princeton-researchers-tested-radiative-cooling-with-natural-ventilation-and-thermal-mass-keeping-a-building-3-9c-below-outdoor-air/articleshow/133754059.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133754153,imgsize-1315083.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pine martens vanished from England for a century; locals helped bring them back, now 4 kits spotted]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133755103.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/pine-martens-vanished-from-england-for-a-century-locals-built-den-boxes-and-set-up-cameras-to-track-their-return-now-four-kits-have-been-spotted/articleshow/133755103.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/pine-martens-vanished-from-england-for-a-century-locals-built-den-boxes-and-set-up-cameras-to-track-their-return-now-four-kits-have-been-spotted/articleshow/133755103.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T12:50:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133755376,imgsize-2240066.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Removing some fish helped a degraded Chinese lake begin to recover]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133755878.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-removed-just-2040-of-fish-from-a-degraded-chinese-lake-underwater-plants-and-water-clarity-began-recovering/articleshow/133755878.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-removed-just-2040-of-fish-from-a-degraded-chinese-lake-underwater-plants-and-water-clarity-began-recovering/articleshow/133755878.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T13:14:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133756019,imgsize-294078.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Refugee at 9, US Army veteran, Yonas Hagos became a top Arby's franchisee]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133754965.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-9-yonas-hagos-arrived-in-america-from-a-sudan-refugee-camp-years-later-he-became-a-major-arbys-franchise-owner-after-serving-in-the-us-army/articleshow/133754965.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/at-9-yonas-hagos-arrived-in-america-from-a-sudan-refugee-camp-years-later-he-became-a-major-arbys-franchise-owner-after-serving-in-the-us-army/articleshow/133754965.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T12:50:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133755199,imgsize-927266.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[5-year-old leaves Texas school unnoticed; stranger finds him]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133755589.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A five-year-old student left Rufino Mendoza Elementary School unnoticed during school hours. A good Samaritan found the crying child several blocks away and returned him. The school initially claimed staff had retrieved the student before he left campus. The child's mother stated the school did not fully disclose the incident details. She is now seeking legal action and fears for her son's safety.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-mom-says-school-told-her-staff-caught-her-5-year-old-son-she-later-learned-a-stranger-found-him-crying-two-blocks-away/articleshow/133755589.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/texas-mom-says-school-told-her-staff-caught-her-5-year-old-son-she-later-learned-a-stranger-found-him-crying-two-blocks-away/articleshow/133755589.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T13:07:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133755804,imgsize-272551.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists recreated a 17th-century perfume made to remember its creator's mother]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133745239.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/scientists-recreated-a-17th-century-perfume-from-a-forgotten-recipe-researchers-think-it-was-made-to-remember-its-creators-mother/articleshow/133745239.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/scientists-recreated-a-17th-century-perfume-from-a-forgotten-recipe-researchers-think-it-was-made-to-remember-its-creators-mother/articleshow/133745239.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T05:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133745239,imgsize-89276.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Canada planted a pine forest over a rare savanna; removing it restored nature]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133746016.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canada-planted-a-pine-forest-where-a-rare-savanna-once-stood-removing-the-trees-later-brought-back-a-richer-ecosystem/articleshow/133746016.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/canada-planted-a-pine-forest-where-a-rare-savanna-once-stood-removing-the-trees-later-brought-back-a-richer-ecosystem/articleshow/133746016.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T10:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133746229,imgsize-302534.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[FBI adds India-origin man Manjit Singh Bedi to most-wanted fraudsters list, offers reward up to $150k for info]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133753946.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The FBI has placed Manjit Singh Bedi on its most-wanted list due to accusations of fraudulent activities amounting to over $600,000 in government benefits. Allegedly exploiting customer EBT cards for cash instead of food, Bedi fled to Canada and then to India following criminal charges. A significant reward is being offered by the FBI for any information that could lead to his capture.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/nri/us-canada-news/fbi-adds-india-origin-man-manjit-singh-bedi-to-most-wanted-fraudsters-list-offers-reward-up-to-150k-for-info/articleshow/133753946.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/nri/us-canada-news/fbi-adds-india-origin-man-manjit-singh-bedi-to-most-wanted-fraudsters-list-offers-reward-up-to-150k-for-info/articleshow/133753946.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T12:53:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133755473,imgsize-525209.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Retired repairman built wind-powered sculptures; his park now draws 194,300 visitors, $5.3 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133751896.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A retired North Carolina farm machinery repairman turned scrap metal into towering wind-powered sculptures, creating a collection that became a local attraction. After his 30 restored whirligigs were moved to downtown Wilson, the Vollis Simpson Whirligig Park opened in 2017. The park has since become a cultural and economic draw, recording about 194,300 visitors in 2024 and generating an estimated $5.3 million in regional sales annually.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-retired-north-carolina-repairman-built-giant-wind-powered-sculptures-from-scrap-after-30-were-moved-downtown-the-park-drew-194300-visitors-and-generated-5-3-million-in-regional-sales/articleshow/133751896.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-retired-north-carolina-repairman-built-giant-wind-powered-sculptures-from-scrap-after-30-were-moved-downtown-the-park-drew-194300-visitors-and-generated-5-3-million-in-regional-sales/articleshow/133751896.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133752270,imgsize-137595.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Do trees have their version of muscles? This is what scientists say]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133754295.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/trees-have-their-own-version-of-muscles-scientists-discover-how-they-sense-a-tilt-and-straighten-themselves-a-lesson-in-how-nature-finds-its-balance/articleshow/133754295.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/trees-have-their-own-version-of-muscles-scientists-discover-how-they-sense-a-tilt-and-straighten-themselves-a-lesson-in-how-nature-finds-its-balance/articleshow/133754295.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T12:31:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133754952,imgsize-923756.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[South Florida teens use pizza and tech to fight hunger, delivering 25,000 slices to food deprived families]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133753217.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Meet a passionate brother and sister team from South Florida who launched Pizza for a Purpose, an app aimed at alleviating hunger. This unique platform unites generous donors, local pizzerias, and community organizations, leading to the distribution of over 25,000 pizza slices to families. Their philanthropic journey also includes establishing the Dhanam Foundation, which aims to expand their outreach and charitable efforts significantly.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/south-florida-teens-are-using-pizza-and-technology-to-fight-hunger-in-america-delivered-25000-slices-to-families-in-need/articleshow/133753217.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/south-florida-teens-are-using-pizza-and-technology-to-fight-hunger-in-america-delivered-25000-slices-to-families-in-need/articleshow/133753217.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T12:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133753294,imgsize-118627.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Illinois businessman built a giant wind chime to attract visitors, then made 12 Guinness records]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133751163.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Jim Bolin transformed struggling Casey, Illinois, with giant attractions. What began with a record-breaking wind chime grew into 21 oversized objects and 12 Guinness World Records titles, drawing visitors and national attention to the small town.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2011-illinois-businessman-jim-bolin-built-a-record-breaking-wind-chime-to-draw-travelers-into-casey-15-years-later-his-project-had-grown-to-21-giant-objects-and-12-guinness-records/articleshow/133751163.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2011-illinois-businessman-jim-bolin-built-a-record-breaking-wind-chime-to-draw-travelers-into-casey-15-years-later-his-project-had-grown-to-21-giant-objects-and-12-guinness-records/articleshow/133751163.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T12:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enc