 emerge at Hopewell Museum; reopening set for December 2026]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133751053.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Hopewell Museum is embarking on a remarkable restoration project for its historic house. Careful attention is being given to preserve original elements such as the floors and windows while integrating modern systems to enhance protection of the museum's collections. This comprehensive renovation aims to ensure the building is well-prepared for future use, with a reopening slated for late 2026.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-1877-new-jersey-house-has-served-as-a-museum-since-1924-after-102-years-a-1-5-million-restoration-is-reviving-its-hidden-19th-century-floors-and-preparing-it-to-reopen/articleshow/133751053.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/an-1877-new-jersey-house-has-served-as-a-museum-since-1924-after-102-years-a-1-5-million-restoration-is-reviving-its-hidden-19th-century-floors-and-preparing-it-to-reopen/articleshow/133751053.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T10:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133751077,imgsize-1419986.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Michigan farmer protects his family’s 131 acres from future housing development]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133747546.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Michigan farmer John Boyer bought back his family’s 131 acres after the land changed hands over decades. In 2026, he sold its development rights to the Little Traverse Conservancy through a conservation easement, ensuring the property cannot be divided for housing or commercial development. Boyer hopes the farmland remains protected for generations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-farmer-bought-back-the-131-acres-his-family-had-lost-over-the-decades-in-2026-he-sold-the-development-rights-so-the-land-can-never-be-broken-up-for-housing/articleshow/133747546.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-michigan-farmer-bought-back-the-131-acres-his-family-had-lost-over-the-decades-in-2026-he-sold-the-development-rights-so-the-land-can-never-be-broken-up-for-housing/articleshow/133747546.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-04T03:52:08+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133748302,imgsize-104841.cms"/></item></channel></rss>